>I don't mean to offend NetHack; just I thought that if we wanted to
>have a great game, we could point on the multidungeon functionality.
>What's your opinion?

First of all, Nethack already *is* a great game.

Secondly: It would make the game take longer to play without really
adding anything.  If the dungeons that currently exist are boring, then
adding a wilderness will not magically make them interesting again.
Mostly it will serve to annoy the player by making them travel *even
further* to get from one dungeon to the next - not only will you have to
climb through the dungeon you're currently in, you'll also have to
traipse across /n/ miles of wilderness.

ADOM's wilderness is (just about) bearable purely *because* it is of
fixed geometry.  The two Angband variants I can remember as having
random wildernesses, Cthangband and Zangband, both sometimes produce
wilderness layouts that can render an otherwise promising game far too
painful to continue.
